+## 2026-11-03
+- **Payments a fraction of a cent short no longer need a person** ([#62](https://github.com/trysarathy/investigation-desk/pull/62)). Some wallets and exchanges round away the last fraction of a cent when they send. A payment request that receives up to 0.01 less than it asked for is now treated as paid in full ("matched") instead of "short", with a line saying it was within the rounding tolerance. Shortfalls above 0.01 still go to a person, as before.
+
 ## 2026-11-01
 - **CHANGELOG started.** From today every merged pull request adds an entry here.
